---
description: Rules for the Supabase server (migrations and SQL tests)
globs: supabase/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Never edit an existing migration file that has been committed. Add a new, timestamped
  migration instead.
- The API is RPC-only: new tables get RLS enabled with no policies and no grants to
  anon/authenticated; new RPCs are `SECURITY DEFINER`, `set search_path = public, pg_temp`,
  derive the caller via `idl_private.require_uid()`, and are explicitly granted to `authenticated`.
- Errors use `idl_private.fail('PTxxx', message, field)` so PostgREST returns HTTP xxx.
- Any privacy-behaviour change must update the Kotlin `PrivacyFilter` first, regenerate
  `contract/privacy_vectors.json` (`-Pidl.updateGolden=true`), and make
  `supabase/tests/run.sh` pass.
